h 165af590169e4972's binary has get_duid which is DHCPv6-specific. get_duid exists in dhcp6c (KAME dhcp6c). And sub_40F0F8 with vsprintf + system — in KAME dhcp6c, there's \"script\" execution via system(). Actually dhcp6c executes /etc/dhcp6c-script. There's a known vuln in dhcp6c: command injection via option processing? The args for dhcp6c: `dhcp6c [options] interface`. Options include `-f` (config file), `-c configfile`, `-d`, `-D`, `-r` (rapid commit?)... In KAME dhcp6c, `-r` is \"request certain information\" and there's also `-i`? Let me read the main function.\n\nLet","stream":true,"block":0}

