Historic TP-Link httpd vulns (Archer C7): /cgi command injection? This httpd is a newer \"wmnet/uclibc\" based one? The callees list \"LoginRpmHtm\", \"httpGenListFind\" — this looks like the older TP-Link \"httpd\" (from \"tplink httpd 1.0\"?). Known CVEs: CVE-2014-9585? For Archer C7 v2 with httpd: there were CVEs like CVE-2018-... Let me not rely on memory; instead examine httpd dispatcher: it routes by \"httpGenList...\" (generic list of URL→handler). Let me read httpDispatcher full and find the registration table (route list) via httpGenListInit etc.\n\nB. dhcp6s (UDP 547, likely bound on LAN): server6_recv parses attacker DHCPv6 client packets → option parsing (dhcp6_get_options), duidcpy, hostconf matching, sub_403DCC etc. Memory corruption potential. Also the earlier \"sys_run_command\" wrapper sub_40F0F8 — callers unknown. Let me use fw_search on the dhcp6s binary for function names like \"script\" or find cross-references to sub_40F0F8. fw_call_trace returned empty — maybe direction \"in\" failed because callers couldn't be resolved. Let me try again with direction both.\n\nC. dhcp6c (md5 ae35a5...) — client, receives server replies; known KAME dhcp6c option parse vulns (CVE-2011-0764: dhcp6c stack overflow in get_option? Actually CVE-2011-0764 was \"dhcp6c insufficient validation of DHCPv6 messages\"). But note identification lists dhcp6c's port as TCP null — the input classification is odd; dhcp6c is a client (outbound), and its \"external input\" is DHCP server replies on UDP 546. The trace harness is HTTP GET oriented... The dynamic verifier (fw_request_trace) works via qemu-user with an HTTP GET trigger? Let me check what fw_request_trace does: \"qemu-user differential coverage trace (baseline vs one trigger HTTP GET)\". It needs argv+port+request_path and binary_md5. So the harness can run e.g. httpd with a GET request. For dhcp6s, argv would be \"dhcp6s eth0\" style... request_path maybe unused for non-HTTP binaries? Hmm, it says \"HTTP GET\". For UDP binaries this may not fit; but we can still try with request_path being something and port.\n\nLet me first do the static analysis of httpd (primary, port 80) and dhcp6s (P0 scored).\n\nRead httpDispatcher full source; then find handler registration (httpGenList is a generic list; there's likely cfg table with URL → handler fn). Let me search functions in httpd binary: pattern \"httpCgi\", \"GoIndex\", \"LoginRpmHtm\" etc.\n\nAlso check AS-AUTH docs for httpd auth (AS-AUTH-001..005). Let me fetch those too.\n\nBatch:\n1. f","stream":true,"block":0}

