data: {"seq":267,"ts":"2026-08-22T15:58:57.132Z","text":"Findings so far:\n\n1. dhcp6s sub_40F0F8 = `system(vsprintf(buf, format, args))` — command execution wrapper.\n   - sub_40F168 calls sub_40F0F8 with format \"echo \\\"====>>>>%s\\\" > /dev/ttyS0 \\r\\n\" where %s is first arg.\n   - get_duid calls sub_40F168(\"[%s]wan_if:%s\\n\", \"get_duid\", aEth02). aEth02 = some global string. Let me check what aEth02 is — probably \"eth0.2\" or from config. Not directly user controlled unless interface is set by attacker.\n   \n   So sub_40F0F8 usage is debugging echo to ttyS0 — not a direct network-triggered cmdi. The P0 path \"main → get_duid → sub_40F0F8\" uses fixed strings; the AI review's \"format 可能受 argv/网络控制\" seems over-stated for this particular edge. But sub_40F0F8 might be called elsewhere in the DHCPv6 packet processing (e.g., in react_* handlers) — the call graph only shows get_duid and sub_40F168 as direct callers, so no network path to system(). So the dhcp6s \"command injection\" is not really exploitable via network — unless the interface name or config file affects aEth02. Not externally reachable. Note this in triage but don't record as finding without evidence.\n\n2. httpd sub_425CB8 — delegates to sub_425AA4 or sub_42595C depending on dword_5E69E4 state (auth config). Let me read those two functions.\n\n3. etc/init.d not found. Let me browse the firmware root to find layout: etc/, web/ or www/ dirs.\n\nNext steps:\n- Browse firmware root, www dir listing.\n- Read httpd sub_425AA4 / sub_42595C (auth gates) and httpSystemRpms / dword_5C20C8 registration. Where is the URL→handler table? In httpDispatcher, method table dword_5C20C8 handles \"httpMethods[2* method +1]\" → probably list of {url, handler}. The registered handlers include LoginRpmHtm, GoIndex. Let me search httpd for \"httpRpmRegister\" or \"httpGenListAdd\" calls... Actually, easier: search for functions with \"Rpm\" names and the specific handler that processes login/cgi: \"LoginRpmHtm\". And look for \"cgi\" related: many TP-Link httpd versions have /cgi/luci? no.\n\nLet me use fw_search on pattern \"LoginRpm\" and \"GoIndex\" to get their addresses, then find","stream":true,"block":0}

