 And look for \"cgi\" related: many TP-Link httpd versions have /cgi/luci? no.\n\nLet me use fw_search on pattern \"LoginRpm\" and \"GoIndex\" to get their addresses, then find callers (the init that registers handlers is usually a big function calling httpRpmRegister with URL strings — we can't see strings, but we can look at httpRpmFs, httpHelpRequestRpm, LoginRpmHtm, GoIndex).\n\nAlternatively, minidlnad? No, focus httpd.\n\nActually, maybe better approach for httpd: find the dispatcher's cfg table function. Let me check where dword_5C20C8 is set. Search for \"httpGenListInit\" or \"httpGenList\"? Let me search httpd by pattern \"httpGen\".\n\nAlso let me look at the www/ directory to enumerate RPM pages — httpd serves .htm from the RPM FS via httpRpmFs, and the \"handlers\" are the rpm functions. The famous TP-Link vulns in this era: \"webAddCommand\"? Hmm.\n\nLet me also take a different, higher-value route: the udp inputs (dnsproxy, bpalogin, athadhoc) often have simpler parsing bugs. But first, httpd dispatcher details.\n\nBatch:\n1. fw_browse_firmware root (list).\n2. fw_search \"httpGenListInit\" job_id.\n3. fw_get_function_source httpd 0x425aa4.\n4. fw_get_function_source httpd 0x42595c.","stream":true,"block":0}

