data: {"seq":175,"ts":"2026-08-22T16:05:28.470Z","text":"httpd main is at 0x420584. The qemu trace failed. Let me consider why: perhaps httpd requires special argv (TP-Link httpd often needs to run with \"-f\" foreground, or reads /tmp/web config; but more likely the harness issue is that httpd is a MIPS big-endian binary with some unsupported syscall, or it daemonizes immediately.\n\nActually rc=125 in many harnesses (e.g., EMBA/emux-style docker runners) = \"the command could not be executed\" — often due to missing dynamic linker for qemu. httpd's libs: lib/libpthread.so.0, lib/libc.so.0, lib/librt.so.0, lib/libmsglog.so, lib/libutil.so.0, lib/libwpa_ctrl.so, lib/libgcc_s.so.1. These are in the squashfs \"lib\" dir. Maybe the harness's qemu-user needs LD_LIBRARY_PATH that includes the squashfs lib dir — usually these harnesses set it from the identification's processing_chain libs. Unclear.\n\nAnother possibility: httpd's main checks argv: many TP-Link httpds in this gen require writing pid file etc. — no.\n\nLet me look at httpd main (0x420584) briefly","stream":true,"block":0}

