ecode (0x42faf4) — decodes attacker base64 into a buffer with size arg; logic: writes bytes at a2+v6 with bounds check `if (v6 + 2 - v20++ < v4)` — v4 = a3 = max size. Writes only when index < size. BUT the final `*(a2+v6)=0` writes at index v6 UNCONDITIONALLY. v6 = (v8/8 + v6) where v8 accumulates bits. If v6 >= a3 → the terminator write overflows! Let me examine: with input of many 'A' (4 base64 chars → 3 bytes), v6 increments by 3 each quad. a3 = max output size passed by caller (e.g., in httpPwdDecode: a2 is the decoded buffer, a3=64","stream":true,"block":0}

