e 4096 input buffer (dns_read_packet buffer). Ugh, a1 offsets: a1+255 = qname buffer (256 bytes), a1+324 = raw query → strncpy 0xFF → fine. a1 + 524*i + 2944: i < something; 2944+524*i within 4096. Probably safe.\n\nBetter to fuzz the *network input parsing* of dhcp6s (server6_recv → dhcp6_get_options, sub_403DCC, etc.) or bpalogin's receive/parse (extract_valueINT2, receive_transaction parse) which are compact.\n\nAlso libavformat ff_udp_set_remote_url/udp_open (memcpy ai_addrlen into fixed context) — the URL is parsed via av_url_split; fuzzing \"ff_udp_set_remote_url(buf,url)\" with huge URL — but ai_addrlen comes from getaddrinfo result (the socket addr), not attacker-controlled length; the memcpy size = sizeof(sockaddr) (16 for v4). \"v5->ai_addrlen\" for a resolved host is 16 or 28 — bounded. AI review overstated. Skip.\n\nLet me fetch dhcp6_get_options in dhcp6s and look at the option parsing internals for a memcpy/strcpy with unchecked len. Also grab dhcp6c's similar parser (client side receives server packets — the true \"network input\" of dhcp6c).\n\nRetry \"/\" trace first (maybe slot free now), plus read dhcp6_get_options.","stream":true,"block":0}

