data: {"seq":264,"ts":"2026-08-22T16:18:17.611Z","text":"httpBufferGet returns *(a1+something) presumably — 4 lines; likely `return *(a1+44)` or similar (the response buffer pointer). Callers of httpRpmFs unresolved. This is too speculative to record a finding.\n\nDecision time on where to invest remaining budget. The minidlnad trace is STILL occupying the slot (6+ min). Let me poll it once more; if still running, I'll consider that the slot is stuck and continue static-only, then finalize with an honest summary (no fabricated findings).\n\nActually — maybe the minidlnad run hung because minidlna forks scanner/subprocess and qemu-user's coverage harness waits for ALL processes to exit (a fork child that never exits → run never completes). That would explain both the hang AND block.\n\nAlso possible: it's not stuck; the harness waits for the HTTP GET response with a long timeout because minidlna didn't bind (no interface/config) and the GET just times out, extending the run. Either way, poor target.\n\nGiven: (a) function-fuzz infra broken for mips; (b) httpd GET rejected by harness; (c) minidlnad trace hanging; the dynamic budget effectively can't deliver crash/diff evidence this session. \n\nThe honest outcome: \n- No vulnerability with dynamic verification can be recorded (record_finding requires evidence + trace_id only for observed/verified; static-only is capped 0.7 and allowed without trace — but I must have a SOLID static vuln first, and I don't have one with a clean sink on a public input).\n\nWait — actually, let me reconsider dhcp6s more surgically for a REAL static vuln. The server6_recv relay path (sub_4065B4): it processes relay-forward messages, using `dhcp6_vbuf_copy(v25+13, v117)` etc. v23 = v87[0] (inner message length); `v7 = &v34[v23]` (advance). It allocated v24 (relay info 0x3C). dhcp6_vbuf_copy(v25+13, v117) — copies the inner message (v87) into the relay info buffer. The inner message buffer v87[0] is attacker-length (from relay payload), could be up to ~1450. v25+13 is inside 0x3C-byte alloc — dhcp6_vbuf_copy likely allocates. Also `v34 = (char *)v25[14]` — the copied message; then `v7 = &v34[v23]` — end of inner message; then parses `v112 = v25[14]; v0 = v23; ... dhcp6_get_options(v112+4, v7, v81)` — v7 here is *v34+v23* — but v34 is the inner message buffer which is v23 bytes; so v7 = v34 + v23 = end — good; passing (v112+4, v112+v23) as bounds — consistent if message starts at v34+4? Hmm v112 = v25[14] = v34 = inner message (from dhcp6_vbuf_copy at v25+13?). Inner message = DHCPv6 header (type + 3-byte xid) + options. dhcp6_get_options(v112+4, end) — options start at +4. Bound = v34+v23. OK.\n\nPotential real bug: **unbounded recursion/loop**? The while(1) loop in relay handling repeats for each relay message (up to hop count?) — no hop count limit but 4096 buffer bounds it.\n\nActually, there's one classic KAME dhcp6s issue: in server6_recv for unicast checks etc. — nothing clearly exploitable from decomp.\n\nHonestly, without a concrete bug, discipline says: don't record. Deliver a summary with PoCs/work notes.\n\nBUT — the user explicitly wants \"拿到 qemu 差分或 fuzz 结果后再决定是否入库\" — they instructed to decide based on those results. The results: \n1. httpd 两条 trace：差分 0，触发均为 connection reset（harness 层面无法驱动 httpd 请求处理）→ 无法动态证实登录/命令注入路径可达。\n2. AFL fuzz：mips hook 编译失败，无法运行。\n3. minidlnad trace：挂起中。\n\nSo the correct decision: 不入库任何没有动态证据或过硬静态证据的 httpd 漏洞；已辨明的高分路径（dhcp6s system 包装、xl2tpd、libavformat memcpy）均为误报/不可达。\n\nWait — but before finalizing, let me make sure the minidlnad trace eventually finishes (it affects the slot and final status). Also double-check the \"interesting\" dhcp6s sub_40F168 aEth02 value — is aEth02 maybe from nvram/config (attacker-influenced via DHCP options?)? aEth02 is probably \"eth0.2\" (global). get_duid's third param is the *interface name* from argv (dword_43C600 = argv[optind]) — command line only.","stream":true,"block":0}

