 documented.\n- Mention the minidlnad stuck trace and that fuzz infra broken.\n- Be honest: 没有确认漏洞入库。\n\nWait — before concluding, maybe try one more httpd differential angle: use argv [\"-i\"] (ignore size check → setIgnoreSize; still same). No — the reset is pre-request; argv won't change it.\n\nOne more idea: request_path variations that avoid the harness's TCP problem? No, TCP is TCP.\n\nAlso: perhaps try request on a *different port* for httpd? No.\n\nActually — what if the harness sends the GET to the guest via the *guest's own network namespace loopback* and httpd binds only to LAN interface IP (not 127.0.0.1)? Then connection would be refused/reset! http","stream":true,"block":0}

