ce — not possible for UDP with the HTTP harness). \n\nActually wait — I should double check the claim \"unbounded\": is there any outer length check? v13 = 16-bit field length from datagram (a2+...) — v13-4 bytes copied. No comparison against dest buffer size anywhere. The dests are: a1+1150 (nonce, protocol neg phase) and a1+1174 (server list), a1+12252 (server name). The config struct a1: v35 is a separate 1520+ byte buffer (start_transaction v35 = local array `_DWORD v35[380]` = 1520 bytes + 8 = 1528; v4 = *(+1512) = length). a1 = the config object (~13KB, malloc","stream":true,"block":0}

