.\n- field 0x16 (22) → server list (a1+1174)\n- field 9 → (a1+12252) server name?? Actually that one is after login success (from T_MSG_LOGIN_RESP).\n\n`if ( !extract_valuestring(a1, (int)v35, 0xCu, (char *)(a1 + 1150)) )` — the nonce from auth response. A nonce field > (struct size - 1150) → overflow. Struct size: offsets up to +12772 used → struct ~13KB (a1 allocated 13056?). Nonce would need ~12KB to smash far; but even a few hundred bytes overflow past the intended nonce buffer","stream":true,"block":0}

