ice may not be active by default → reachability caveat: only when service configured/enabled. I'll set reachability static-only, severity medium (~0.5 conf).\n\nHmm, actually — hold on. Let me reconsider whether it's really the *incoming* flow. In receive_udp_transaction, the *incoming datagram* is parsed by sub_402870 → probably dispatches T_MSG types; handle_heartbeats etc. The login() flow is bpalogin acting as *client* to the auth server. The remote attacker controlling data = the auth server (or spoofed). This is fine — the \"external input\" is UDP datagram payload from the server (identification lists bpalogin as UDP public input).\n\nRecord:\n- title: bpalogin 认证响应字段解析未校验长度导致栈/结构溢出 (extract_valuestring unbounded memcpy)\n- vuln_class: 缓冲区溢出 (single class, no slashes → \"内存破坏\" is fine? Rules: SINGLE class, no / 、 ， separators. \"缓冲区溢出\" ok)\n- cwe: CWE-121 (stack overflow is the cleaner claim for v34 token strcpy→ actually the memcpy dests are struct offsets (heap/global) → CWE-122 heap overflow for struct; but the v34 strcpy is stack... two sinks. Pick CWE-121 for v34[200] stack overflow chain: strncpy unbounded into v34[200] then strcpy into slot. Hmm: which is the *primary* sink? extract_valuestring memcpy → writes to struct (heap-like). v34 stack overflow: token = field 0x16 (server list); v18 = strcspn(v34...) — the *first* token of the server list; strncpy(v34, v14, v18) with v18 up to list length (could exceed 200) → stack overflow on v34 + v34[v19]=0. Both matter; CWE-121 fits the stack overflow most cleanly.\n- severity: medium (requires enabled service + on-path spoof)\n- confidence: 0.5 (static-only, reachability uncertain)\n- call_chain: main → mainloop/sub_402870 → login(0x401ab8) → extract_valuestring(0x402bb8) → memcpy 无界 + 栈缓冲 v34[200] strncpy\n  Honestly the exact dispatcher edge from main is unverified in the graph (login has no resolvable callers). Call chain must contain → separators and names/addresses, but I shouldn't fabricate the entry. I can write: \"main(0x40482c) → mainloop(0x401010) → login(0x401ab8) → extract_valuestring(0x402bb8) → memcpy(a4, v11, v13-4) [v13=网络字段长度]\" — mainloop calls... unverified. Risky fabrication. Alternative chain: \"receive_transaction(网络报文入队) → login(0x401ab8)(处理 T_MSG_AUTH_RESP) → extract_valuestring(0x402bb8) → memcpy(a4=固定偏移, v11=报文, v13-4=报文字段长度)\" — receive_transaction fills the buffer from the socket; login consumes. That's honest per decompiled code: login calls receive_transaction and extract_valuestring — the caller-of-login is unknown. I'll word the chain based on confirmed edges: login(0x401ab8) → receive_transaction(网络) → extract_valuestring(0x402bb8) → memcpy 无界；以及 login → strncpy(v34[200], 报文 token, 无界).\n\nActually the call_chain should be 入口到sink. I'll write: \"UDP 认证响应 → receive_transaction(0x403040 接收/解析) → login(0x401ab8) → extract_valuestring(0x402bb8) → memcpy(无界, v13-4 由报文 16 位长度字段控制)\" and additionally \"login(0x401ab8) → strncpy(v34[200] 栈缓冲, token, strcspn 长度无上限) → strcpy(20字节槽)\".\n\nHmm — but reach","stream":true,"block":0}

