ow (single class, no /) — allowed? \"buffer overflow\" has space only. OK.\n- cwe: CWE-121\n- binary_md5: f8a1d1f62eef2e1e73cbbeadd5d51900\n- binary_path: firmware/binwalk_extracted/firmware.extracted/100000/squashfs-root/usr/sbin/bpalogin\n- summary (Chinese), evidence (addresses), confidence 0.6, reachability static-only, call_chain with → inclThe manifest confirms the toolchain: all application binaries (arpping, minidlnad, etc.) have canary:false, nx:false, pie:false, relro:none — this uClibc MIPS toolchain builds no mitigations. bpalogin is in the same toolchain, so canary=false/nx=false is a very safe inference; but to be rigorous I should confirm bpalogin is in the manifest. The manifest is 54KB; the trace of bpalogin could also give checksec. But the manifest","stream":true,"block":0}

