byte ... Let me reconstruct from decomp: start_transaction(v35, type, seq) — v35 is 1520-byte buffer (a2+1512 = length stored at offset 1512). Fields begin at +8 (v6 = a2+8 in extract functions; first field at +8? The transaction buffer: [0]=type, [4]=...? extract walks: v6 = a2+8; reads type at v6[0..1], len at v6[2..3], data at v6+4..; length v4 at a2+1512 (total bytes, must be >=9 initially).\n  So transaction = { u16 type; u16 len(total); then records: u16 ftype; u16 flen; data[flen-4] }? In extract: `v13 = (u16)(*(v11-1) + (*(v11-2)<<8)); memcpy(a4, v11, v13-4)` — v11 = v8+4 (after type word)... v13 read at v11-2 => the length word right before value. So record = u16 ftype + u16 flen + value(flen-4 bytes). The first record starts at +8? Then v4 (=a2+1512) is total message length incl. header 8? initial check v4 < 9 means at least one record.\n  For the PoC: message total = 8 + Σ(4 + (flen-4)) = 8 + Σflen.\n  Login response (type 5): records:\n  - ftype 0x000A (status): flen = 2+4? value is u16 status → flen should be 6 (4+2) so that flen-4=2 bytes data. Hmm record len semantics: \"len\" includes the 4-byte type+len header, data = len-4. extract_valueINT2: v12 = (v9[1]+(*v9<<8)) reads 2 bytes at v9 = record data start. OK.\n  - ftype 0x0016: flen = 4 + N (N bytes of \"AAA...\").\n  The client first sends: protocol neg (recv type 2: response — 2 fields: 0x000A status? plus 0x0018 (24) value string into a1+1020 \"extract_valuestring(a1, v35, 0x18u, (char *)(a1 + 1020))\", 0x0002 protocol=1). Wait in login(): after first receive (type 2 expected):\n    extract_valueINT2(0x0A, a1+1168)  // ","stream":true,"block":0}

