data: {"seq":35,"ts":"2026-08-22T16:32:06.509Z","text":"The user is pressing to record the confirmed entry vulnerability. The manifest.json was truncated at libexec/xtables section — I didn't get bpalogin's checksec entry. But the whole toolchain shows canary:false for every MIPS binary (all seen so far: arpping, busybox, minidlnad, ntfs-3g, libs). uClibc MIPS binaries here have no stack canaries. I'll note that in evidence as toolchain-wide (no canary) — actually I only have explicit checksec for binaries in manifest; bpalogin entry wasn't shown due to truncation. To be safe, confidence 0.6 and mention checksec pattern of the toolchain (all binaries canary:false) — I can reasonably assume bpalogin is same; but the rule says memory-corruption without checksec evidence ≤0.6 — I'll keep 0.6.\n\nNow record the finding: bpalogin login() server-list stack overflow.\n\nDetails:\n- binary: usr/sbin/bpalogin, md5 f8a1d1f62eef2e1e73cbbeadd5d51900\n- function: login @ 0x401ab8 (dupe of the v34 strncpy sink)\n- sink: strncpy(v34, v14, v18) at 0x401ab8 (~line in decomp; the loop `strncpy(v34, v14, v18)`), and extract_valuestring memcpy unbounded (0x402bb8)\n- call_chain: main(0x40482c) → mainloop(0x401010) → login(0x401ab8) → extract_valuestring(0x402bb8, field 0x16) → strcspn/strncpy(v34[200]) → stack buffer overflow\n- cwe: CWE-121\n- vuln_class: stack overflow → but must be SINGLE class without \"/\". \"stack overflow\" ok. Actually server rule: values containing `/`, `，`, `、` rejected. \"stack overflow\" is fine.\n- severity: high\n- reachability: static-only\n- confidence: 0.6\n- evidence: list function evidence addresses (md5+addr strings) + manifest canary notes + trace ids of httpd (not for this finding — evidence for the finding should be static; I can include the traced httpd ids in the summary response, not here)\n- poc: craft UDP Login Response. Need transaction format: add_field_* builds records: 2-byte type + 2-byte len + data; transaction header: 2-byte type + 2-