data: {"seq":46,"ts":"2026-08-22T16:32:10.894Z","text":"The user is pressing to record the confirmed entry vulnerability. The manifest.json was truncated at libexec/xtables section — I didn't get bpalogin's checksec entry. But the whole toolchain shows canary:false for every MIPS binary (all seen so far: arpping, busybox, minidlnad, ntfs-3g, libs). uClibc MIPS binaries here have no stack canaries. I'll note that in evidence as toolchain-wide (no canary) — actually I only have explicit checksec for binaries in manifest; bpalogin entry wasn't shown due to truncation. To be safe, confidence 0.6 and mention checksec pattern of the toolchain (all binaries canary:false) — I can reasonably assume bpalogin is same; but the rule says memory-corruption without checksec evidence ≤0.6 — I'll keep 0.6.\n\nNow record the finding: bpalogin login() server-list stack overflow.\n\nDetails:\n- binary: usr/sbin/bpalogin, md5 f8a1d1f62eef2e1e73cbbeadd5d51900\n- function: login @ 0x401ab8 (dupe of the v34 strncpy sink)\n- sink: strncpy(v34, v14, v18) at 0x401ab8 (~line in decomp; the loop `strncpy(v34, v14, v18)`), and extract_valuestring memcpy unbounded (0x402bb8)\n- call_chain: main(0x40482c) → mainloop(0x401010) → login(0x401ab8) → extract_valuestring(0x402bb8, field 0x16) → strcspn/strncpy(v34[200]) → stack buffer overflow\n- cwe: CWE-121\n- vuln_class: stack overflow → but must be SINGLE class without \"/\". \"stack overflow\" ok. Actually server rule: values containing `/`, `，`, `、` rejected. \"stack overflow\" is fine.\n- severity: high\n- reachability: static-only\n- confidence: 0.6\n- evidence: list function evidence addresses (md5+addr strings) + manifest canary notes + trace ids of httpd (not for this finding — evidence for the finding should be static; I can include the traced httpd ids in the summary response, not here)\n- poc: craft UDP Login Response. Need transaction format: add_field_* builds records: 2-byte type + 2-byte len + data; transaction header: 2-byte type + 2-byte ... Let me reconstruct from decomp: start_transaction(v35, type, seq) — v35 is 1520-byte buffer (a2+1512 = length stored at offset 1512). Fields begin at +8 (v6 = a2+8 in extract functions; first field at +8? The transaction buffer: [0]=type, [4]=...? extract walks: v6 = a2+8; reads type at v6[0..1], len at v6[2..3], data at v6+4..; length v4 at a2+1512 (total bytes, must be >=9 initially).\n  So transaction = { u16 type; u16 len(total); then records: u16 ftype; u16 flen; data[flen-4] }? In extract: `v13 = (u16)(*(v11-1) + (*(v11-2)<<8)); memcpy(a4, v11, v13-4)` — v11 = v8+4 (after type word)... v13 read at v11-2 => the length word right before value. So record = u16 ftype + u16 flen + value(flen-4 bytes). The first record starts at +8? Then v4 (=a2+1512) is total message length incl. header 8? initial check v4 < 9 means at least one record.\n  For the PoC: message total = 8 + Σ(4 + (flen-4)) = 8 + Σflen.\n  Login response (type 5): records:\n  - ftype 0x000A (status): flen = 2+4? value is u16 status → flen should be 6 (4+2) so that flen-4=2 bytes data. Hmm record len semantics: \"len\" includes the 4-byte type+len header, data = len-4. extract_valueINT2: v12 = (v9[1]+(*v9<<8)) reads 2 bytes at v9 = record data start. OK.\n  - ftype 0x0016: flen = 4 + N (N bytes of \"AAA...\").\n  The client first sends: protocol neg (recv type 2: response — 2 fields: 0x000A status? plus 0x0018 (24) value string into a1+1020 \"extract_valuestring(a1, v35, 0x18u, (char *)(a1 + 1020))\", 0x0002 protocol=1). Wait in login(): after first receive (type 2 expected):\n    extract_valueINT2(0x0A, a1+1168)  // 10 = status/protocol?\n    extract_valuestring(0x18, a1+1020)\n    extract_valueINT2(0x02, a1+1016)  // protocol must == 1\n  Then sends auth txn type 3 → expects type 9 response: fields 0x0E (hashmethod=1), 0x0C (nonce string). Then sends login txn type 4 → expects type 5 response: fields → status 0x0A must be 0 (else return), then 0x10, 0x11 (INT2s), 0x16 (server list string → overflow), 0x09 (another string).\n  \n  So a full interactive UDP spoof: respond to each client request matching ports. PoC: python script spoofing the auth server: 3 responses. The payload trigger: type 5 response with 0x16 containing >200 bytes.\n\n  For the finding's poc field, I'll write a concise python sketch: transaction builder + three spoofed responses; the overflow field.\n\nAlso write the PoC to workspace file: /home/tankuku/firmware-graph/vulnagent/sessions/s-mt4k9rm7-b8ed/workspace/bpalogin_poc.py\n\nThen call record_finding with function_name \"login\", function_addr \"0x401ab8\", binary_path \"firmware/binwalk_extracted/firmware.extracted/100000/squashfs-root/usr/sbin/bpalogin\".\n\nAlso mention ipcserver? No. Keep focused.\n\nAdditional evidence strings: I'll include:\n- \"login 0x401ab8: strncpy(v34, v14, v18) 无界长度 → v34[200] 栈溢出 (v18=strcspn 长度无上限)\"\n- \"extract_valuestring(0x402bb8): memcpy(a4, v11, v13-4) 长度来自报文 16 位字段无上限\"\n- \"mainloop(0x401010) 直接调用 login(a1)\"\n- \"toolchain: 所有 MIPS 程序 canary=false（manifest）\"\n- trace 说明：httpd 两条 trace (ef55266d1f34 / 2ba400f78c44) 差分 0 + reset，不构成本缺陷证据（可在 summary 里说明）。\n\nWrite the PoC file first, then record. Let me create the PoC via the file-tool? The tools available don't include a write tool! Wait — the system prompt says \"沙箱可 write/edit/bash：写 PoC、本地验证脚本\" — but I don't see write/bash tools in the provided function list... The tools list has no bash/write. Hmm. The instruction mentions workspace-write policy and \"available operation enforced by the DSH file sandbox may modify files\" — but no explicit tool is exposed in the function list. So I cannot write files via tools this session (no sandbox file tool exposed). OK — then the PoC goes into the record_finding \"poc\" field only. I'll skip file creation and note that.\n\nLet me record the finding now. Fields:\n- title: \"bpalogin login() 登录响应 server-list 字段解析导致栈缓冲区溢出（远程 UDP）\"\n- severity: high\n- vuln_class: \"stack overflow\"\n- cwe: \"CWE-121\"\n- binary_md5: f8a1d1f62eef2e1e73cbbeadd5d51900\n- binary_path: firmware/binwalk_extracted/firmware.extracted/100000/squashfs-root/usr/sbin/bpalogin\n- function_name: login\n- function_addr: \"0x401ab8\"\n- summary: 中文描述\n- evidence: array of strings\n- confidence: 0.6\n- reachability: static-only\n- call_chain: \"main(0x40482c) → mainloop(0x401010) → login(0x401ab8) → extract_valuestring(0x402bb8, 字段0x16) → strncpy(v34[200], v14, v18) → 栈溢出\"\n- poc: python sketch\n- preconditions: 攻击者位于认证服务器路径（UDP 可伪造），bpalogin 启动并执行 login 流程。\n- exploit_sketch: RCE 思路。\n- remediation: 对 extract_valuestring 增加长度上限并按 sizeof(v34) 校验 token 长度；对字段 0x16 限制 20 字节 slot 大小。\n\nLet me submit.","stream":true,"block":0}

