ind 80.\n\nWhat about minidlnad with argv config? The earlier minidlnad failure was \"unsafe library search path\" (ELF RPATH containing build dir) — that's a qemu-user loader rejection. It could be worked around if the trace runner strips RPATH or sets QEMU_... — not under our control. Retry minidlnad maybe? It failed the same way twice (8519f7adc93d). The third attempt (4cfb0cac0b5c) ran (started), so the RPATH issue was fixed by orchestrator restart; but then it hung and was killed. minidlnad hangs because... it forks a scanner child and maybe the parent continues but no HTTP? Actually maybe it DID bind 8200 but the harness GET waits; the run \"hung\" 211s then killed. Timing: it hung at startup... Possibly because minidlnad without config file tries realpath(\"/tmp/mediaserver/cache\")→ make_dir — should work on the sandbox rootfs (writable?). It might block waiting for","stream":true,"block":0}

