event: thinking
data: {"seq":164,"ts":"2026-08-22T16:47:32.979Z","text":"ExecuteStaticRouteTable → sub_43F5C0 (per-route executor). Let me read sub_43F5C0 — that's where a route entry (dest, netmask, gateway, metric...) gets applied, likely via system(\"route add ...\"). If it formats with snprintf and executes — go to finding if attacker-controlled fields reach it via web. But note: routes come from web (httpd) via IPC (sendMsgToHwNat is kernel/hwnat notify). The chain to uclited: httpd's static route page → \"uc\" reader in uclited → ExecuteStaticRouteTable. The web→uclited IPC — data flows through shared memory/msg. Static analysis of cross-process IPC is heavy.\n\nLet me read sub_43F5C0 first.","stream":true,"block":0}

