e... but let me see the loop body where update happens.\n\nActually — hmm, we have limited budget. Let me instead go for a target where verification is achievable: **function-level fuzz** is broken... **frida** is x86-only. **Trace** only HTTP GET. So \"动态\" can only show httpd GET behavior, which resets.\n\nWait — there's one more dynamic idea I haven't tried: fw_request_trace with **argv** pointing to a mode where httpd serves without needing the network stack, e.g. nothing. No.\n\nWhat about **minidlnad** again: it failed with RPATH error, then hung. The RPATH error is a qemu-user safety rejection based on ELF RPATH containing an absolute build path. Some harnesses set QEMU_SET_ENV or strip. Can't control. Skip.\n\nOK — the most defensible additional finding: **httpd Ddns \"cliUrl\" → swDdnsStart → dynStart → sub_53513C (DDNS client)**, IF any of the sub_53xxxx functions call system/tp_systemEx with the stored domain/cliUrl/passwd. Let me read sub_53513C full and sub_533F8C. If none, drop.\n\nAlso **PeanutHull** ph* functions: phRegisterDomainName (0x536580) / phTcpSendRegisterDomain (0x5378d4) — these build HTTP requests (socket), not shell. The earlier swDdnsStart callee list had no system/tp_systemEx. The DDNS chain likely socket-based → no cmdi.\n\nLet me quickly read sub_53513C (full) and sub_533F8C (brief) to close this.","stream":false,"block":0}

