data: {"seq":473,"ts":"2026-08-22T16:50:20.948Z","text":"duidcpy: malloc(v2) + memcpy — safe (heap alloc sized by attacker length; only allocation-size issue, no overflow).\n\nI've now done a thorough pass. Honest conclusion for this round:\n\n**No additional confirmable vulnerability found** in this round beyond the already-recorded bpalogin one. The candidates examined were excluded with real evidence. Record FALSE positives would violate discipline.\n\nStill — the user wants a dynamic+static combo continuation. One more dynamic idea that I haven't actually tried yet this round: **httpd trace with a *query-param-bearing GET*** — e.g., request_path=\"/userRpm/DynDdnsRpm.htm?Save=1&wan=0&provider=1&username=admin&pwd=x&cliUrl=...\" — maybe the reset is because httpd processes GET only with Host header/query? No — reset happens identically for bare \"/\". The harness likely sends \"GET / HTTP/1.0\\r\\n\\r\\n\" — httpd (wmnet) may require \"HTTP/1.1\" + Host (sub_40D1FC minidlna rejected without Host; httpd may too → new_conn closes → RST). If httpd closes the connection with RST on missing Host, the harness gives \"Connection reset\"","stream":true,"block":0}

