data: {"seq":527,"ts":"2026-08-22T16:50:44.955Z","text":"minidlnad trace completed this time (no RPATH error, no hang — the orchestrator restart fixed both). But: **Connection refused on port 8200** — minidlna ran (baseline 40 funcs, tb 1967) but did not bind 8200. Why? Without config/nvram, maybe minidlna binds only after initializing SQLite DB and scanner completes, or it needs an interface (n_lan_addr==0 → binds 0.0.0.0?). Or the bind happens in a *forked child* (CreateDatabase/scanner) not covered. Or it binds on the WAN IP only via lan_addr... With no interfaces in qemu (no eth0), getifaddr fails → n_lan_addr=0 → it might skip binding entirely → connection refused. So minidlna under qemu has no interface → no listen. Harness can't drive it.\n\nConclusion: dynamic coverage channel is fully exhausted for this firmware under current harness constraints:\n- httpd: connection reset (likely new_conn closes on missing \"Host\" header, since harness only sends the URL line; the reset is identical for all paths)\n- uclited/minidlnad: no listener bound (no interfaces/config)\n- UDP services: harness only does HTTP GET\n- fuzz: afl-qemu mips hook compile error\n\nFinal answer for this round:\n1. The single confirmed vulnerability remains F-mt4ljkg4-bede (bpalogin login() server-list 栈溢出) — already recorded.\n2. This round's additional deep-dive results are exclusions (with evidence), no NEW confirmable vuln; I will not fabricate one.\n3. Provide the working \"动\" evidence recap: trace ids 3b662344b97a (minidlna refused), 157e1f694b18 (uclited refused), httpd resets, fuzz fz-2f3b8931 error — all real, all showing the harness cannot reach request processing; therefore no observed/verified-grade upgrade possible, and static exclusions stand.\n\nAlso deliverable: the httpd \"Host header\" hypothesis is my reasoned explanation for the resets — present it as such, not as fact.\n\nThat's the honest, discipline-compliant close. Keep it concise.","stream":true,"block":0}

