data: {"seq":119,"ts":"2026-08-22T16:54:44.440Z","text":"Both fuzz runs are still running (whole-binary fz-86cbf814 started first, function fz-ecec3526 queued after). They'll take up to 120s each. While waiting, let me analyze the dhcp6_get_options input handling to prep crash triage AND check the dhcp6s main's interface-fallback so whole-binary has any chance (ifinit). Actually — instead, use this time productively: examine **dhcp6c** (client, ae35a5...) since its whole network input is server replies; specifically its option parser at 0x40bb8c — IDENTICAL layout to dhcp6s. Known historical dhcp6c bug: in `dhcp6_get_options` there might be non-identical parts. Rather than re-reading all 531 lines, focus on parts where the client differs (they're the same build but separate binaries — the code is a fork). Skip.\n\nBetter use of time: examine **athadhoc** (IN-001, UDP) — small; its recv handler might have a quick, confirmable bug we can tie into a finding with poc. But we don't have fuzz for it and traces can't do UDP... static-only again. Diminishing.\n\nActually — the most productive static-adjacent thing while fuzz runs: pull the **crashes dir** listing for whole-binary run? Can't; no tool. Just poll runs after some time.\n\nLet me also queue the minidlnad \"-i lo\"","stream":true,"block":0}

